# THIS REPOSITORY IS PUBLIC. Everything committed here is world-readable and
# stays world-readable: GitHub serves deleted history for a period, forks keep
# it indefinitely, and mirrors index it within minutes. A secret pushed here is
# a secret rotated, not a secret removed.
#
# So these patterns are not tidiness. They are the standing guard, and they are
# deliberately broader than what has gone wrong so far.

# Key material. The production licence signing key is the single most
# consequential secret in FireFlo -- a database can be restored from backup, a
# signature cannot be forged -- and it must never be inside this tree. It is
# kept outside the repository on purpose.
*.pem
*.key
*.p12
*.pfx
*.jks
*.der
id_rsa*
id_ed25519*

# Environment and configuration carrying real values. conf.example/ inside a
# release tarball is placeholders and ships intentionally; a loose .env here
# would be somebody's actual deployment.
.env
.env.*
*.env
fireflo.env
credentials.yml

# Unpacked release trees. The tarball beside them already holds every byte, so
# committing an extracted copy doubles the repository for nothing -- and an
# unpacked tree is where a prod key gets dropped and forgotten, which is exactly
# how it nearly happened here.
*/gateway/
fireflo-*-linux-*/
!fireflo-*-linux-*.tar.gz

# Local noise
.DS_Store
*.swp
